UID:ned-ned-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260912T080000Z
DTEND:20260912T120000Z
SUMMARY:Ned Ned Run
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating over 40 years\, this race explores the high-altitude trails around Nederland at over 8\,000 feet. Includes a family-friendly 5K road run.
LOCATION:151 East St\, Nederland\, CO 80466
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lead-king-loop-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260913T080000Z
DTEND:20260913T120000Z
SUMMARY:Lead King Loop
DESCRIPTION:A spectacular fall running event through peak fall colors in the Elk Mountains. Participants can run\, hike\, or walk the 25K Lead King Loop past Crystal Mill and through the historic Town of Crystal\, or take on the 8-Mile Quarry Climb along the Yule Marble Quarry Road. Includes post-race BBQ\, beer (21+)\, custom shirt\, and finisher medal. Kids 2.5K fun run around Beaver Lake. Benefits Marble Charter School.
LOCATION:TBD
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:run-rabbit-run-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260918T090000Z
DTEND:20260918T130000Z
SUMMARY:Run Rabbit Run
DESCRIPTION:The Run Rabbit Run features two ultramarathon races: the 14th Annual 100 Mile Race on September 18\, 2026 (limited to 450 entrants with Tortoise and Hare divisions) and the 19th Annual 50 Mile Race on September 19\, 2026 (limited to 200 entrants). The 100 mile race offers the highest purse of any 100 mile race with $100\,000 overall ($20\,000 to winners). Registration is currently full; waitlist available. A charity race benefiting northern Colorado nonprofits.
LOCATION:Steamboat Ski Resort\, 2305 Mt Werner Cir\, Steamboat Springs\, CO 80487
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-ascent-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260919T080000Z
DTEND:20260919T120000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Ascent & Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Pikes Peak Marathon\, founded in 1956 and the oldest continually held marathon in the United States\, takes runners from Manitou Springs\, Colorado\, to the summit of Pikes Peak at 14\,115 feet and back down for a total of 26.2 grueling mountain miles. The sister race\, the Pikes Peak Ascent\, is a 13.3-mile climb to the summit via the historic Barr Trail on the east face of the mountain\, gaining approximately 7\,800 vertical feet.
LOCATION:441 Manitou Ave\, Suite 100\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:run-the-rockies-road-race-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260919T080000Z
DTEND:20260919T120000Z
SUMMARY:Run the Rockies Road Race
DESCRIPTION:The 50th Annual Run the Rockies Road race features a downhill course along the Summit County Recreation Path through Ten Mile Canyon. The 11k course (100% downhill) starts at 8:30 AM\, and the Half Marathon course (75% downhill) starts at 8:00 AM. Both races showcase beautiful fall foliage and have a hard stop at 11:30 AM. Registration opens April 22\, 2026. Includes commemorative gifts\, finisher items\, aid stations\, professional timing\, post-race food\, and post-race beer (21+).
LOCATION:Starts near Copper Mountain\, ends at Frisco Historic Park\, 1 Main Street\, Frisco\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fall-equinox-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260920T080000Z
DTEND:20260920T120000Z
SUMMARY:Fall Equinox Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Fall Equinox is a multi-day race event held in Fort Collins\, CO\, running from September 20 through October 3\, 2026. It features a Half Marathon and 5 Mile distances.
LOCATION:Fort Collins\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pikes-peak-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260920T070000Z
DTEND:20260920T110000Z
SUMMARY:Pikes Peak Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Known as 'America's Ultimate Challenge\,' this race ascends to the 14\,115-foot summit of Pikes Peak before descending back to Manitou Springs. It is one of the most physically demanding marathons in the world due to the 7\,800-foot vertical climb.
LOCATION:Manitou Ave (City Hall)\, Manitou Springs\, CO 80829
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:golden-leaf-half-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260926T080000Z
DTEND:20260926T120000Z
SUMMARY:Golden Leaf Half Marathon
DESCRIPTION:The Golden Leaf Half Marathon is a 13.3-mile trail race traversing from Snowmass Village to the heart of Aspen on mountain trails and roads. Chosen by Trail Runner Magazine as one of 'America's 14 most scenic races' and by Colorado Runner as a Best Half Marathon\, this race showcases Colorado's breathtaking fall colors at peak season. Registration includes race entry\, lunch\, t-shirt\, bar\, and prize giveaway. Mass start format with no waves. Note: A valid CORSAR (Colorado Outdoor Recreation Search and Rescue) card is required by Pitkin County for participation.
LOCATION:Snowmass Village to Aspen\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:west-line-winder-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260926T080000Z
DTEND:20260926T120000Z
SUMMARY:West Line Winder
DESCRIPTION:The West Line Winder 30K & 50K features miles of buttery single track and forest roads with glorious views of the Collegiate Peaks\, set on arid desert-style trails just outside of Buena Vista\, CO. Suitable for first-time trail runners to veteran ultramarathoners. Hosted by 14er Fest\, the event includes trail events\, clinics\, festival camping\, live music\, local libations\, and vendors.
LOCATION:Buena Vista\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:crested-butte-ultra-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260726T000000Z
DTSTART:20260926T060000Z
DTEND:20260926T100000Z
SUMMARY:Crested Butte Ultra
DESCRIPTION:Hosted during the peak of autumn\, this trail race treats runners to golden aspen groves and expansive mountain vistas. The course uses flowy singletrack and challenging terrain around one of Colorado's most famous mountain towns.
LOCATION:Crested Butte Mountain Resort\, 12 Emmons Rd\, Crested Butte\, CO 81225
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
